{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2022983","formula":"C₈H₁₀N₂O₃S","hill":"C8H10N2O3S","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":10.0,"N":2.0,"O":3.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sulfacetamide","ru":"Сульфацетамид","uk":"Сульфацетамід"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sulfacetamide is a sulfonamide antibiotic commonly used in the treatment of bacterial infections, particularly those affecting the eyes and skin. It functions by inhibiting the synthesis of folic acid in bacteria, which is essential for their growth and reproduction, thereby exerting a bacteriostatic effect. Available in various forms, including eye drops, topical solutions, and creams, sulfacetamide is often prescribed for conditions such as conjunctivitis, seborrheic dermatitis, and acne vulgaris.","ru":"Сульфацетамид (устар. «Альбуцид») — противомикробное бактериостатическое средство, относится к классу сульфаниламидов. Является промежуточным продуктом синтеза стрептоцида.","uk":"Сульфацетамід — синтетичний антибактеріальний препарат з групи сульфаніламідних препаратів для місцевого застосування."},"fame":26,"pubchemCid":5320,"mass":214.24,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=O)NS(=O)(=O)C1=CC=C(C=C1)N","inchikey":"SKIVFJLNDNKQPD-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-(4-aminophenyl)sulfonylacetamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5320","atoms":24,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.167,"y":-1.275,"z":-0.248,"el":"S"},{"x":1.171,"y":-2.585,"z":0.389,"el":"O"},{"x":1.589,"y":-1.151,"z":-1.637,"el":"O"},{"x":2.43,"y":1.511,"z":-0.874,"el":"O"},{"x":2.094,"y":-0.193,"z":0.706,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.276,"y":1.075,"z":0.202,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.431,"y":-0.585,"z":-0.117,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.282,"y":-0.989,"z":0.912,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.857,"y":0.37,"z":-1.04,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.985,"y":0.517,"z":0.095,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.559,"y":-0.